2025-05-01 03:44:01 - Thread-1610 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "APP_GROUP_ID": identifier of the application group – we must group results by this column.  
• "USER_ID": unique identifier of a user – we have to count the distinct values per day.  
• "TIME": numeric (‑epoch‑seconds) moment when the session started – use it to isolate the June 1 → June 7 2023 window and to derive the calendar “start‑day”.  
• (Optional) "SF_CREATED_AT": already a TIMESTAMP_LTZ which can help to double‑check the day derived from "TIME".

Typical filters / conditions you will need  
• WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 /* 2023‑06‑01 00:00:00 UTC */  
                 AND 1686182399 /* 2023‑06‑07 23:59:59 UTC */  
• or, if you feel safer with the timestamp column: WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT"::DATE BETWEEN '2023‑06‑01' AND '2023‑06‑07'  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (each capped to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final aggregation you will eventually need.

```sql
-- 1. Description: quick look at the raw data (20 rows only)
SELECT 
  "USER_ID",
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "TIME",
  "SF_CREATED_AT"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: list of distinct app‑group IDs available
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "APP_GROUP_ID"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: check distinct calendar days present in the June‑1→June‑7 window,
--                 deriving day from epoch seconds
SELECT DISTINCT 
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
ORDER BY "session_day"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: sample of users who started sessions on 2023‑06‑03
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "USER_ID",
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) = '2023-06-03'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: distinct users per app‑group across the 7‑day window
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "USER_ID"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: add the derived day and keep 20 example rows
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "USER_ID",
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: count unique users per (app_group, day); simple GROUP BY, 20 rows
SELECT 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "USER_ID")         AS "unique_users"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
GROUP BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME"))
ORDER BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: same as #7 but through a CTE, still limited to 20 rows
WITH june_sessions AS (
  SELECT 
    "APP_GROUP_ID",
    "USER_ID",
    TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day"
  FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
  WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
)
SELECT 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "USER_ID") AS "unique_users"
FROM june_sessions
GROUP BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day"
ORDER BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: use QUALIFY + RANK to pick one row per (user, day, app_group)
WITH ranked AS (
  SELECT
    "APP_GROUP_ID",
    TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day",
    "USER_ID",
    RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY "APP_GROUP_ID", "USER_ID",
                            TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME"))
                 ORDER BY "TIME") AS r
  FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
  WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
)
SELECT 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day",
  COUNT(*) AS "unique_users"
FROM ranked
WHERE r = 1
GROUP BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: approximate distinct count variant (HLL), example output capped
SELECT
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME")) AS "session_day",
  APPROX_COUNT_DISTINCT("USER_ID")  AS "approx_unique_users"
FROM BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC."USERS_BEHAVIORS_APP_SESSIONSTART_VIEW"
WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685577600 AND 1686182399
GROUP BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP_LTZ("TIME"))
ORDER BY 
  "APP_GROUP_ID",
  "session_day"
LIMIT 20;
```
